Subject: [PATCH] avutil/tx: free the sub-transform array of a failed codelet

A codelet init such as ff_tx_dct_init() or ff_tx_rdft_init() calls
ff_tx_init_subtx() on its own context, which allocates that context's
sub array, and can then fail. reset_ctx(sctx, 0) keeps sctx->sub for the
next codelet attempt, so when no attempt succeeds the array is lost when
s->sub is freed. Free it there.

Found by failing each allocation of a binkaudio_dct decoder open in turn:
an allocation failure in ff_tx_dct_init() or ff_tx_rdft_init() leaked
one TX_MAX_SUB * sizeof(AVTXContext) block.
---
 libavutil/tx.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavutil/tx.c b/libavutil/tx.c
--- a/libavutil/tx.c
+++ b/libavutil/tx.c
@@ -892,8 +892,10 @@
             break;
     }
 
-    if (!s->nb_sub)
+    if (!s->nb_sub) {
+        av_freep(&s->sub[0].sub);
         av_freep(&s->sub);
+    }
 
 end:
     av_free(cd_matches);
